      "worked_solution": "First, we find $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xyz+{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =2xz+3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $g_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xz+3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xyz}(1,2,3) & =2(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
